WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.126
A man: Allahu Akbar. Allahu Akbar.

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:09.437
Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah

00:00:09.795 --> 00:00:13.484
Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah

00:00:14.437 --> 00:00:18.364
Hayya Alal Salat. Hayya Alal Salat

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:23.960
Hayya Alal Falah. Hayya Alal Falah

00:00:25.628 --> 00:00:29.756
Allahu Akbar. Allahu Akbar.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.895
A man: La Elaha Ella Allah

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: Alhamdu Lillah, Wa Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:59.000
This first Khutba will link up with the Khutbas that Dean Majul has been giving us.

00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:06.542
And before I start, I would like to draw your attention to something that we probably take for granted,

00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:13.542
and that is, here is a mosque that advocates the worship of Allah alone.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:22.083
I know that God sent Moses to preach La Elaha Ella Allah, as we know in Sura 21,

00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:24.677
and not to preach the glorification of Moses.

00:01:25.497 --> 00:01:31.000
And God sent Jesus to preach the worship of God alone, La Elaha Ella Allah,

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.361
and not to preach the glorification of Jesus.

00:01:34.406 --> 00:01:39.580
And God sent Muhammad to preach the worship of God alone,

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.722
and not to preach the glorification of Muhammad or anyone else.

00:01:44.451 --> 00:01:46.045
Just worshiping God alone.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.000
In this mosque, we advocate the worship of God alone, and we follow the Quran to the letter.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.767
We came to call this mosque the University of God, because it is the most important education,

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:06.993
and we have been very fortunate in seeing the truth of the Quran and sticking to every letter of it.

00:02:08.587 --> 00:02:13.774
The University of God, the most important education,

00:02:13.774 --> 00:02:17.000
lacked official professorship.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:25.722
So, you can see from God's vantage point, He said, well, these people are advocating the worship of Me alone, God alone,

00:02:25.722 --> 00:02:27.173
and they need a professor.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.406
So, let's send them a professor.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.684
So, God appoints a couple of angels to go and hunt for the best professor on earth.

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:41.730
And He gets us not only a professor, but a Dean of the Islamic Institute in the Philippines.

00:02:44.903 --> 00:02:47.865
Dr. Khalifa: Now, he doesn't know why he is here in Tucson.

00:02:48.678 --> 00:02:49.730
Dean Majul: (unintelligible)

00:02:53.729 --> 00:02:58.451
Dr. Khalifa: All he knows is, he sit down in Tucson, he got stuck to the Masjid Tucson.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:06.000
And he's teaching us, bless his heart, and he's been teaching us about Adam and Eve and the sin of Adam and Eve.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.677
And we've been enjoying his teachings, so we have an official,

00:03:11.677 --> 00:03:16.000
not just any professor, the Dean himself,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.000
of an official school, so we, we don't lack officialdom in here.

00:03:22.271 --> 00:03:27.271
What Dean Majul has been teaching us, the last few Khutbas of his, were the sin of Adam and Eve.

00:03:27.271 --> 00:03:29.129
What was the sin of Adam and Eve?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.316
They ate from the tree.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.181
That's what they did.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:41.000
And because they ate from the tree, they did not qualify to continue in Jannah, in Heaven, in Paradise,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.000
the Kingdom of God.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.271
Because they ate from the tree.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
They committed one sin.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.226
What does this teach us? What do we learn from this important lesson?

00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:56.316
We learn that you cannot go to Jannah with one sin.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.000
If you have one sin in your record, you do not qualify to go to Heaven.

00:04:03.729 --> 00:04:04.729
Sounds difficult.

00:04:05.007 --> 00:04:08.729
But for the people who worship Allah alone, it is not difficult at all.

00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:12.000
Because there are two ways of wiping out the sins from your record.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.000
And this means, nobody will see them, you will not see them in the record,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.226
if you fulfill these two requirements.

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:26.091
But the thing we must learn, from Dean Majul's lessons in the past,

00:04:26.091 --> 00:04:30.310
that Adam's and Eve's sin is, they ate from the tree, they were kicked out.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.406
Because they committed one sin.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.851
Therefore, we learn from this, that we cannot go to Heaven with one sin on our record. Not one.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:47.316
If you commit one sin, and you have it in your record, then you will die,

00:04:47.316 --> 00:04:48.767
you cannot go to Heaven.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.813
You must be absolutely sinless.

00:04:51.813 --> 00:04:56.445
Because when Adam and Eve ate from the tree, they didn't commit murder.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.271
You know, they ate from the tree.

00:04:58.594 --> 00:04:59.594
That's all they did.

00:04:59.781 --> 00:05:04.677
God told them, you go on Heaven, and eat from anything you want, but not this one tree.

00:05:06.302 --> 00:05:08.406
They ate from the tree, and they were kicked out.

00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:12.451
And this is exactly what we're doing here on this earth.

00:05:15.361 --> 00:05:25.000
We are here to be tested, and to end this life without a single sin in your record.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Otherwise, you do not qualify to join the Kingdom of God,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.000
you do not qualify to enter Jannah.

00:05:32.122 --> 00:05:38.451
Now, how do we, what are the ways of erasing sin from your record?

00:05:39.406 --> 00:05:40.917
Now, this is one thing you must remember.

00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:46.045
You must, must never forget that our goal is to end this life without a single sin.

00:05:49.361 --> 00:05:50.639
How can we do that?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.587
The first method of erasing sin is Tawbah, repentance.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.000
That's one thing.

00:05:58.625 --> 00:06:02.361
You turn to God and you say, I'm sorry, I made a mistake, I will never do it again.

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:09.677
I pledge, I will never do it again, I repent, I'm sorry, I apologize.

00:06:10.271 --> 00:06:12.271
All the words of apology that you can muster.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
And you pledge solemnly that you will not do it again.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.000
That's one way.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.316
What if your repentance is not acceptable?

00:06:21.684 --> 00:06:24.399
There comes the second way. The second way is to pay for it.

00:06:26.264 --> 00:06:29.497
The first way to erase sins is, is Tawbah, repentance.

00:06:29.497 --> 00:06:33.046
And the second way is to pay for them here in this world.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.497
And they are very expensive, I'm telling you.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:48.000
I would like to, to put a, a dollar value on the sins and how you pay for them here in this world.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.361
Now, as a believer, you will pay in material things.

00:06:51.361 --> 00:06:54.264
Thank God, you do not pay with your arm or your leg or...

00:06:54.264 --> 00:06:58.167
Just look around this mosque, you don't see anyone with one arm or one leg, Alhamdu Lillah.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.226
You have to say Alhamdu Lillah every time.

00:07:01.226 --> 00:07:10.768
But, you will, when I put material values in it, it seems like the punishment is out of proportion for the sin.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.135
But you have to pay for it, if, unless you wanna, you want it in your record.

00:07:15.135 --> 00:07:20.309
Dr. Khalifa: If you want one, if you have one sin on your record, you cannot go to Jannah.

00:07:21.528 --> 00:07:27.573
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:07:27.573 --> 00:07:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: People go and commit adultery, and they think it's a simple matter.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.587
Well, marriage is really a simple matter.

00:07:39.587 --> 00:07:43.445
If you have a relationship with another person, you might as well want to suggest marriage.

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:50.000
It's very simple, two witnesses, you call Allah, you declare that you're married.

00:07:50.594 --> 00:07:55.000
But if you fall into adultery,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.323
Dr. Khalifa: my dollar value on it is ten thousand dollars.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.323
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:07:59.497 --> 00:08:01.233
Dr. Khalifa: You have to pay

00:08:01.233 --> 00:08:04.684
in misery, or if you don't have the ten thousand dollars, it will be in problems.

00:08:06.316 --> 00:08:12.316
The payment for sins seems to be out of proportion in this world, but really it isn't.

00:08:12.316 --> 00:08:13.316
It's a tremendous mercy.

00:08:13.736 --> 00:08:19.135
So, the believers are the only people who enjoy certain problems in this world,

00:08:19.135 --> 00:08:22.541
because they know they are paying for certain, wiping out certain sins.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:30.000
The believer does not get away with sins in this world, he has to pay for it.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:36.000
The disbeliever doesn't either, except with the disbeliever, the punishment continues in the Hereafter.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:43.238
With the disbeliever, the punishment in this world, it also comes in this world, but he or she cannot make the connection.

00:08:44.914 --> 00:08:46.961
They will appear to get away with sin.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.755
And then, after years, months, after a time when the person cannot connect

00:08:52.755 --> 00:08:55.000
the punishment with the sin, bang!

00:08:56.437 --> 00:08:57.444
They get hit.

00:08:59.477 --> 00:09:09.000
So, the two ways to erase sins are repentance and paying for them.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.563
These are the only two ways.

00:09:12.238 --> 00:09:19.556
There's one sin, not sin, it's not even a sin, there's one offense that cannot be forgiven.

00:09:19.556 --> 00:09:24.278
The only unforgivable offense, I will let you open the Qurans, now read from your Qurans,

00:09:24.278 --> 00:09:27.278
and get Sura 39, verse 53.

00:09:28.722 --> 00:09:31.722
No, excuse me, I made a mistake, 4:48.

00:09:32.642 --> 00:09:34.642
Dr. Khalifa: Not even that, 4:17.

00:09:35.357 --> 00:09:36.642
A woman: (unintelligible)
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:38.000
A man: What Sura?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: 4:17 is page 53.

00:09:43.278 --> 00:09:45.841
Alright, this is the order God wants us to see.

00:09:48.185 --> 00:09:51.834
This is not the one that I wanted to do, but it deals with repentance.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.437
Page 53, verse 16 says,

00:09:58.477 --> 00:10:11.064
[4:17]  Repentance is accepted by GOD from those who fall in sin due to ignorance, then repent immediately. GOD redeems these. And GOD is Knower, Wise.

00:10:11.603 --> 00:10:14.159
So, this is how repentance, repentance is accepted.

00:10:14.159 --> 00:10:15.000
Let's go on.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:30.000
[4:18]  But repentance is not acceptable from those who continue to commit sins until death comes to them, then say, "Now I repent." Nor is it acceptable from those who die as disbelievers. We have prepared for these a painful retribution.

00:10:30.285 --> 00:10:34.278
So, repentance, there are conditions for accepting Tawbah, for accepting repentance.

00:10:34.523 --> 00:10:36.682
That you fall in sin due to ignorance.

00:10:37.801 --> 00:10:40.563
In other words, you don't know that wine is Haram,

00:10:40.563 --> 00:10:42.000
and you go drink wine.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.318
Then, you find out in Quran that wine, liquor, alcohol is Haram.

00:10:47.755 --> 00:10:49.000
Then, you repent.

00:10:49.563 --> 00:10:51.238
And you pledge you'll never do it again.

00:10:51.238 --> 00:10:53.000
You made a mistake, you'll never do it again.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Then, you repent and it's accepted.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:00.238
But if you know that wine, liquor, whiskey, marijuana, or any of those is Haram,

00:11:00.238 --> 00:11:02.841
and you go deliberately and you do it, you cannot repent from that.

00:11:02.841 --> 00:11:03.841
You have to pay.

00:11:03.841 --> 00:11:05.278
And the price is very high,

00:11:05.278 --> 00:11:07.397
either here, or there.

00:11:08.794 --> 00:11:12.788
If you know that adultery is Haram, and you go commit it,

00:11:12.788 --> 00:11:14.199
you cannot repent from that.

00:11:14.199 --> 00:11:16.510
There is no repentance there. You have to pay.

00:11:17.477 --> 00:11:19.795
And the pay is very expensive, ten thousand dollars.

00:11:19.795 --> 00:11:22.596
You know, the prostitutes are down there for fifty dollars or a hundred or something.

00:11:23.318 --> 00:11:29.000
But the price that you pay, according to God's law

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.715
is, I put a figure on it, just roughly, ten thousand dollars.

00:11:33.437 --> 00:11:35.636
In misery, or problems, or whatever.

00:11:37.556 --> 00:11:39.556
So, this is the condition for repentance.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.430
You can repent only if you fall into sin due to ignorance, and then repent immediately.

00:11:46.358 --> 00:11:47.683
You can't linger.

00:11:48.358 --> 00:11:51.000
In the right way, you say, I'm sorry God, I made a mistake.

00:11:52.516 --> 00:11:55.198
That's, that's, these are the conditions for repentance.

00:11:56.437 --> 00:11:59.437
Also, let's go to 39:65.

00:12:01.199 --> 00:12:04.517
Because when I say you cannot go to Heaven with one sin,

00:12:04.517 --> 00:12:06.000
it sounds terrible, doesn't it?

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.159
Not one sin.

00:12:08.159 --> 00:12:11.000
Because Adam and Eve ate from the tree, just committed one sin.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.437
39:65.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.206
Dr. Khalifa: Sura Al-Zumer

00:12:19.437 --> 00:12:20.563
A man: What's the page?

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:25.788
Dr. Khalifa: 319. Page 319, verse number 65.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.642
No, that's not the one.

00:12:29.238 --> 00:12:30.238
53.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.318
Excuse me, it's on the same page anyway.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.000
53.

00:12:35.682 --> 00:12:36.301
It says,

00:12:36.301 --> 00:12:47.061
[39:53]  Say to My servants who exceeded the limits, never despair of God's mercy. GOD forgives all sins. For He is the Forgiver, the Merciful."

00:12:48.325 --> 00:12:50.643
Now, the Arabic is even a lot stronger.

00:12:50.643 --> 00:12:56.391
قُلْ يَعِبَادِىَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَىٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا مِن رَّحْمَةِ ٱللَّهِ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا (39:53)

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.762
All sins. God forgives all sins.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.404
Moses committed murder.

00:13:02.563 --> 00:13:03.563
But he was forgiven.

00:13:04.318 --> 00:13:09.622
If you remember the Quran, Moses immediately turned to God and said, this is the act of the devil, please God forgive me.

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:11.318
He repented immediately, didn't he?

00:13:11.556 --> 00:13:13.722
And he didn't intend to kill the man either.

00:13:14.516 --> 00:13:17.039
But he was forgiven right there in the same prayer.

00:13:18.516 --> 00:13:20.000
The same verse of the Quran.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.000
So, God forgives all sins.

00:13:23.596 --> 00:13:26.722
The instruction here for us is never to despair from God's mercy.

00:13:28.953 --> 00:13:31.039
There is one unforgivable offense.

00:13:31.039 --> 00:13:33.516
Now, that's the one in 4:48.

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:38.556
Let's go to 4:48.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.834
Down at the bottom of the page, it says,

00:13:50.834 --> 00:13:53.318
Idol worship, the only unforgivable offense.

00:13:53.914 --> 00:14:07.170
[4:48] GOD never forgives the idolization of anything besides Him,* and He forgives all lesser offenses for whomever He wills. Anyone who sets up any idol besides GOD, has forged a gross blasphemy.

00:14:07.766 --> 00:14:10.596
Therefore, the only unforgivable offense is idol worship.

00:14:10.914 --> 00:14:14.795
And this is why we are very careful in this mosque not to idolize anyone,

00:14:14.795 --> 00:14:20.516
not Mary, not Jesus, not Muhammad, not Moses, not any, not any saint, not anyone, not anything.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.000
Our motto is Allah alone.

00:14:25.318 --> 00:14:27.318
And the criterion is in the Quran.

00:14:30.417 --> 00:14:30.947
that

00:14:30.947 --> 00:14:33.901
إِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ ٱشْمَأَزَّتْ قُلُوبُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ (39:45)

00:14:33.901 --> 00:14:35.901
When you talk about God alone, they don't like it.

00:14:37.358 --> 00:14:38.564
That's the sign, but we love it.

00:14:38.921 --> 00:14:40.166
We talk about Allah alone.

00:14:40.722 --> 00:14:43.722
Because idol worship is the only unforgivable offense.

00:14:53.397 --> 00:14:55.874
That's a goal in the same,

00:14:55.874 --> 00:15:00.000
in the same Sura, verse 116, 116.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.523
It is page 63.

00:15:05.722 --> 00:15:08.199
Again at the bottom of the page, it says,

00:15:08.199 --> 00:15:20.422
[4:116] GOD does not forgive the idolization of any idols besides Him (if maintained until death),* and He forgives all lesser offenses for whomever He wills. Anyone who idolizes any idol besides GOD has gone far astray.

00:15:21.477 --> 00:15:24.835
So, now we know that there is only one

00:15:24.835 --> 00:15:27.523
unforgivable offense, and that is idol worship,

00:15:27.523 --> 00:15:30.000
to idolize anyone or anything.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.762
Just the one that is not forgivable.

00:15:31.762 --> 00:15:35.239
Because the whole idea of creating us in this world

00:15:35.239 --> 00:15:37.000
is to worship Allah alone.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.000
And this is why we are told throughout Quran

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.801
that the prophets have no power to benefit you or harm you,

00:15:45.801 --> 00:15:48.198
have no power to benefit themselves or harm themselves.

00:15:48.198 --> 00:15:49.603
Why is God saying that?

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Why?

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.682
Because the people have tendency to idolize their leaders,

00:15:54.682 --> 00:15:56.411
their saints, their prophets.

00:15:57.801 --> 00:16:00.404
Christians idolize Jesus, the Muslims idolize Muhammad.

00:16:01.596 --> 00:16:03.206
The Shia idolize the Imams.

00:16:04.596 --> 00:16:06.000
It's a plague.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.318
It's a plague that, that Satan set up

00:16:09.318 --> 00:16:11.642
for the Jews, the Christians and the Muslims.

00:16:11.642 --> 00:16:12.768
And people fall in it.

00:16:13.642 --> 00:16:16.357
And we find it reflected in the Quran, a statement of fact.

00:16:16.357 --> 00:16:19.000
(12:106) وَمَا يُؤْمِنُ أَكْثَرُهُم بِٱللَّهِ إِلَّا وَهُم مُّشْرِكُونَ

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.477
The majority of believers fall in idol worship.

00:16:24.139 --> 00:16:26.298
(12:103) وَمَآ أَكْثَرُ ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتَ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ

00:16:26.298 --> 00:16:28.397
The majority of people will not believe to start with,

00:16:28.397 --> 00:16:31.238
and the majority of the minority will fall in idol worship.

00:16:31.874 --> 00:16:36.622
This is why you must be absolutely positive and careful that you are idolizing no one,

00:16:36.622 --> 00:16:38.397
that you are worshiping Allah alone,

00:16:38.397 --> 00:16:41.993
that you are following the Quran alone,

00:16:41.993 --> 00:16:43.484
the words of Allah alone.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.470
You don't accept any instructions from anyone because God is the Wisest.

00:16:54.225 --> 00:16:59.332
So with this in mind, we know that all sins are forgivable.

00:17:01.477 --> 00:17:04.404
The only unforgivable offense is idol worship.

00:17:05.437 --> 00:17:08.437
And we know that we cannot go to Heaven with one sin.

00:17:08.437 --> 00:17:11.332
We must erase all sins.

00:17:13.636 --> 00:17:16.636
When we die, we mustn't have one sin in our record.

00:17:16.636 --> 00:17:20.000
